t(1, 720, """The truth is the opening of the file of the whole Ummah .. A 20-year-old girl in Pakistan was accused of adultery without witnesses, and without being given a chance to defend herself .. A dangerous file whose title is: a section of the Muslims invent a new religion that the Prophet ﷺ and his family never brought, embrace it and enforce it by force of arms, throwing against the wall the words of their Lord, the Mighty, the Compeller, the King, and His commands and prohibitions, and invent punishments and hadd penalties of their own!!""")

h(1, 1300, """The killing of the Pakistani Khalida Shandio: Reopening the file of the tribal councils and the sins and crimes of these councils!""")

t(1, 1990, """To those whose prayers have been delayed in being answered for years while they wait, there are several matters: among people are those whose prayer is answered with better than what they asked, in Paradise, so what is better than what they asked for in this world is stored up for them. And there are those whose prayer is answered after a year, or five years, or ten years, or twenty years. Whoever finds that the answer to his prayer is delayed, let him know that there are those whose answer was delayed even longer! I have an experience of patience in the answering of prayer that I relate, perhaps the reader may benefit: between the years 2015 and 2016 I went through an extremely difficult, bitter experience; it demolished all my previous life completely, not partially, and my current life that I live today actually began in 2017 as a clear, steady life line with no crookedness in it.

When the years 2015 and 2016 were extremely heavy and represented an unprecedented distress, the period from mid-2015 to mid-2016 was a stage of great striving in the night-prayer supplication; I left nothing I wished for in this world and the Hereafter except that I asked for it from the Lord of the worlds, the King, the Great, holy are His names and attributes, exalted in the heavens and the earth, and highly exalted. And as is the habit of weak man, he calls on his Lord and hopes for the answer while his soul waits, but something happened that changed the equation!

In November 2016, in Malaysia - the station of the land of distresses, as it represented three visits for three great distresses - in that month of 2016, while I was at the station of the second distress""")

t(2, 60, """(2010 - 2016 - 2024), carrying in my chest many prayers I had made to our Great Lord, I saw in a dream the Prophet ﷺ standing on a platform about 5 cm above the ground, while I sat directly in front of him. To my right and left were men all dressed in white, strangers I did not know, with meters between me and them to the right and left (perhaps 5 meters). The Prophet ﷺ addressed us all together and said what I want the reader to understand now, and it is the essence of the experience .. I had prayed for much, and the dream did not come for me alone, but for other Muslims too, so that the Prophet ﷺ addresses us with one address, saying: "You have been answered in everything you prayed for, but in its time."

This great dream was a major turning point in my understanding of the decrees of Allah the Exalted. I understood, learned and realized that it is not right for us, nor fitting, nor permissible, nor our right, nor expected of us, nor is our Lord pleased with us, that we hasten the answer, or insist on its hastening, or question the reason for its delay; that all this is error, mistake and lack of understanding, and failure to grasp the will of Allah the Exalted in His servants and in the earth we live on, where we live the decrees of the Great Lord.

For this reason I no longer hasten. In ten years, 1 to 10% of the prayers were answered, and Allah knows best. The reason for not knowing how much of the prayer was answered is that man is so ignorant of the unseen of Allah hidden from him in his own life; a real ignorance that confirms the reality of the creature's worth of nothingness before the decrees of Allah the Exalted on him, such that he may not even be able to calculate precisely how much of his prayer was answered. In view of all this, as a lowly servant of Allah the Exalted, poor before Him, I continue to pray with most of the same prayers since that dream (2016 - 2026), a little less than ten years having now passed since it. For it is never fitting for us to cut off prayer, and it is never right for us to cut off our entreaty to the Great Lord, even if we were given glad tidings that our prayers were answered. For the answer is one matter, and continuing the prayer is another. However long the answer is delayed, call upon Allah the Exalted, and do not stop even if you are given glad tidings that your prayer has been answered. Do not hasten, do not get angry, do not sigh, do not resent, and do not despair, lest you stop praying, abandon the great worship of supplication, and become one of the regretful.""")

h(2, 1300, """Allah is with the patient. To those who hasten the answer to prayer and are not patient!""")

t(2, 1990, """My son, my daughter: take it from me, and cut short the pains that are certain for everyone who resents the will of Allah on earth!
We are two creations; we do not resemble each other in dozens of things. A man who looks at a woman and sees himself with a woman's face is mad, and a woman who looks into the mirror and finds herself with a man's face is mad!

Allah the Exalted created us two creations, not one creation .. Hundreds of millions of men and women lived, then died and left this world without knowing what I am saying!

What I am saying is knowledge that one is obliged to know; it is not a luxury of knowledge, nor a pattern of amusement with optional reading! The matter is great; it is the cause of the corruption of the minds of most women and the corruption of the minds of most men!

The man who thinks that Allah the Exalted created the woman's soul like his own soul is a man who needs to learn the obligatory knowledge; and the woman who thinks that Allah the Exalted created the man's soul like her own soul is a woman who needs to learn the obligatory knowledge!

Ignorance has struck most people a blow, ruined them, and wiped out their minds, leaving them without understanding, perception, comprehension or knowledge. Ignorance covered them and became their cloak, and wisdom was withheld from them, so they dwelt in the abode of those who wronged themselves. Allah did not wrong them; all this is because their Lord commanded them to learn, yet they refused anything but ignorance""")

t(3, 110, """We are two creations: in soul we do not resemble each other, in mind we do not resemble each other, and in desires we do not resemble each other; there is nothing common between us except perception and conscience!""")

h(3, 600, """Life is not a game; Allah's testing of us is not a picnic. Our Great Lord created us with measures and attributes, and whoever does not understand this creation will not be able to change the will of Allah on earth""")

h(3, 1700, """In life one is either a policeman or a thief. As for the half policeman, half thief, woe to people from him! Woe, then woe, then woe""")

t(3, 2280, """And how many returning women will on that day threaten their families in the homelands with what is not good, because of the greatness of what they did in the West! They made great creative works there! Be creative!

Protection from exemplary punishment is a right!""")

t(4, 965, """They do not love those who give advice .. They marry forbidden marriages, and toy with religion, honor and dignity .. O fathers, brothers and families .. What is happening is not a lawful marriage! Do you understand the meaning of these words? These are void, invalid marriage contracts! Clean up your lives, since you have reached this extent of frivolity! Clean up your lives by repenting to Allah your Great Lord, and by teaching these girls, after their divorce, the religion, jurisprudence and the Shariah.""")

h(4, 1500, """"He keeps away from the cameras on religious occasions, but appears on other occasions" 🤷🏻‍♀️ — "My cousin married a Christian and he became Muslim, and in the end he divorced her because his heart was not at ease with Islam; it was just a pretext to marry her\" """)

t(4, 2195, """So that it be one of the greatest trials, and one of the hardest tests absolutely""")

h(5, 300, """No chosenness happens through human effort; it is a divine choice, pure, pure, pure""")

t(5, 740, """If the mind does not grasp a quarter of things, it is impossible for it to grasp all things. Many people see before their eyes examples of humans who do not understand even part of something, to the point of foolishness, and they spend their lives waiting for them to understand everything, and this will not happen except by a miracle!""")

h(5, 1200, """What is not grasped in part is not grasped in whole!""")

t(5, 1860, """From the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stirred in his sleep, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something in your sleep you did not use to do. He said: "Strange! People of my Ummah will head for the House because of a man of Quraysh who has taken refuge at the House, until when they are at al-Bayda they will be swallowed by the earth." We said: O Messenger of Allah, the road gathers all people. He said: "Yes, among them are the one who knows, the one compelled, and the wayfarer; they perish in a single destruction, and emerge from different sources; Allah will resurrect them according to their intentions."» Sahih Muslim""")

h(5, 2300, """To this group of the people of the Levant: you will bid farewell to your children, your spouses, your fathers and your brothers, and then you will never see them again!""")

t(6, 590, """To the travelers in that time and that era which does not resemble our time today: do not take the road between Mecca and Medina on that day! Pay attention to a dangerous wording in the hadith in Muslim!

((Among them .. the wayfarer)), meaning the traveler ..

The traveler, at the time the land army marches, will be forced either to join the army of the swallowing, or to march with it merely for the sake of marching .. Then the earth will open up and they will all sink into it!

From the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stirred in his sleep, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something in your sleep you did not use to do. He said: "Strange! People of my Ummah will head for the House because of a man of Quraysh who has taken refuge at the House, until when they are at al-Bayda they will be swallowed by the earth." We said: O Messenger of Allah, the road gathers all people. He said: "Yes, among them are the one who knows, the one compelled, and the wayfarer; they perish in a single destruction, and emerge from different sources; Allah will resurrect them according to their intentions."» Sahih Muslim""")

h(6, 1600, """Warning: in the future time of people's lives""")

t(6, 2160, """"You have returned to where you began, you have returned to where you began" Sahih Muslim .. The story began at Siffin, and we have been living the story for 1400 years, and the end of the story is in a desert plain (bayda) of the earth, and this is one of the meanings of "you have returned to where you began"!

As everything began, it ends with the same old attempt .. Siffin will not return .. and the results of Siffin will not be repeated! The coming Siffin is the swallowing! You will enter Siffin in a different way .. You will carry a banner of misguidance and march under it, so take what holds salvation for whoever of you wants salvation!

O youth of the Levant: some of you will be called to a banner of misguidance. If you are able to flee on that day, do so; and if you cannot, then march under it with the march of one compelled, forced, grieving, bidding farewell to his family, for you will not see them except on the Day of Resurrection!""")

t(7, 60, """From the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stirred in his sleep, so we said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something in your sleep you did not use to do. He said: "Strange! People of my Ummah will head for the House because of a man of Quraysh who has taken refuge at the House, until when they are at al-Bayda they will be swallowed by the earth." We said: O Messenger of Allah, the road gathers all people. He said: "Yes, among them are the one who knows, the one compelled, and the wayfarer; they perish in a single destruction, and emerge from different sources; Allah will resurrect them according to their intentions."» Sahih Muslim""")

h(7, 650, """"You have returned to where you began, you have returned to where you began." The beginning of the story was Siffin, and the end of the story is a desert plain of the earth. O youth of the Levant, listen""")

t(7, 1300, """Indeed, O people of the Levant, tomorrow is not like yesterday; so let every flatterer fear Allah regarding himself! And do not do what the grandfathers did .. beware""")

h(7, 1800, """From Siffin to a desert plain of the earth: a banner of guidance and a banner of misguidance. The beginning of the story and the end of the story""")

t(7, 2385, """The balance of the heart between steadiness, shaking and severing

Today's recording, by the power of Allah the Exalted .. The balance whose steadiness means the steadiness of the rope of connection with Allah the Exalted, whose shaking means the shaking of the rope of connection with Allah the Exalted, and whose crashing means the severing of the rope between the servant and his Lord!""")

t(8, 80, """This balance exists .. Eyes do not see it, but understandings grasp it, and the experience of the greater jihad (the jihad of the soul) reveals it .. It is the reason someone asks about a righteous man who went astray: why did he go astray after his righteousness? And about a misguided man who became righteous: how did he become righteous after he was misguided?

The image: the water beneath the heart means the heart being surrounded by trials, and a rope connecting the heart and the sky, and in the middle the balance that weighs the movement of what is finer than a hair when it shakes!""")

h(8, 1750, """If I lacked humility, and then it were sold for the earth's fill of gold, I would buy it and not care""")

h(9, 350, """Whoever Allah placed in a decree and then "decided by his own mind" to reject the decree, and did not understand the meaning of the Great One's ruling, does not reason. He will call out in the darknesses! Because he rejected the ruling of the Great One""")

h(9, 1300, """My Lord does not challenge with the strong, nor with the rich, nor with the master of his people, nor with the mighty among people. But my Lord challenges with the weak, the poor, the one despised among his people, and the lowly among people!""")

t(9, 1910, """Or all of them!

People talk about celebrities they worked with, saying that so-and-so, and so-and-so, and such-and-such a woman, and so-and-so, who presented themselves to people in the image of the reformer, the pure and the wise, were among those who are arrogant on earth toward simple people!""")

h(9, 2350, """Among the causes of conceit: forbidden wealth consumed, or abject ignorance, or an injustice one has become entangled in!""")

h(10, 900, """The conceited and the arrogant is abandoned by his Lord, but he does not know it!""")

t(10, 1610, """When the streets are completely closed and walled, with a private gate inside a closed city, and the owners of the villas and palaces in it agreed when buying their properties on 🟢🟢((((their being partners in the streets of the closed city, and their ownership not being limited only to the villas and palaces they bought))))🟢🟢, then the jurisprudential characterization of the issue of the residents of the larger city outside the walls of the closed city of the wealthy sharing in their private city is governed by the rules of "common private ownership" and the system of "easements" in Islamic jurisprudence.

1. The jurisprudential ruling on closed streets (private shared roads)

* Their ownership: these streets do not take the ruling of "public roads" in jurisprudence; rather they are a private shared road (or common ownership) owned by the owners of the properties inside this wall by virtue of purchase and use contracts.
* The right of disposal: the maintenance, lighting and cleaning of these streets fall financially on the owners, and therefore the "right of easement" is established for them in jurisprudence, along with the right to regulate entry to them to protect their privacy and property.
* The rule of preventing harm: the owners have the right in jurisprudence to prevent the entry of non-residents or those not permitted, based on the jurisprudential rule: "No one may dispose of another's property without his permission", and the rule "Harm is to be removed" (if the influx of strangers causes crowding that prevents the rightful owners from benefiting from their streets, shops and restaurants inside the wall).

2. The jurisprudential ruling on the shops inside the closed compound

* The ruling on entering the shops: the shops inside the walled compound are treated in jurisprudence according to "general permission" or "special permission", explicitly or by custom:
* If they serve only the residents: the owners or the compound management have the right to bar non-residents from entering them through the main gate, because the shop lies within land under common private ownership.
* If the gate is opened to the general public: if the compound management or the shop owners themselves allow the general public to enter in order to profit from them and increase earnings, then the wealthy have no right to be angry here, because the shop owner disposes of his property in a way that does not harm the structure of the compound, and here the rule applies: "The owner""")

t(11, 60, """disposes of his property as he wishes, as long as he does not cause gross harm to others."

3. The balance between the financial right and the moral appearance

* The legitimacy of privacy: it is the Shariah right of the wealthy to buy properties that provide them with calm, privacy and security, and the Shariah does not prevent a person from enjoying his lawful wealth in a closed environment, as he ﷺ said: "Of the happiness of the Muslim: a spacious dwelling and a righteous neighbor."
* The missing moral criterion: the desire for distinction and privacy is lawful in jurisprudence, but the error of these wealthy people lies in the "psychological motive" (which is anger at people not being their equals in class); the Shariah permits them to prevent entry based on "legal and financial right and privacy", but it condemns prevention based on "contempt for the poor and arrogance over them".""")

h(11, 900, """The jurisprudential characterization of a wealthy man's anger at the poor entering a closed city of the wealthy!""")

t(11, 1560, """Real life is not the falseness of appearance from outside, while the very soul of the one who errs, loves errors and persists in them is burnt, melted and torn apart from within, making a great effort to cover up his state. But everyone who understands knows the truth, for they are exposed truths in society, not a secret!""")

h(11, 2000, """What is right is hundreds of things, and human dignity has a costly price, which is living rightly. Whoever has tried it has lived a life the lovers of errors and deficiencies know nothing about!""")

h(12, 500, """No creature will feel that it respects itself from within unless it does what is right and adheres to it! How many who persist in errors despise themselves and do not show it to people!""")

h(12, 1600, """The difference between the God-fearing and the wretched is that the God-fearing lived what Allah made lawful in their homes, while the wretched lived what Allah made lawful in the streets!""")

t(12, 2190, """Between the Yusuf of 2023 and the Yusuf of 2026

As is my habit, if a matter worries me by day or in the evening, I wait for the night prayer, because I "always" read from the Mushaf by opening it at random. And as is my habit, I am used to the Mushaf opening at the right-hand page from which I begin the recitation, so that the page and the one facing it answer the question posed in my mind about the matter. Is the same thing always happening for long years a coincidence? The answer is no, because this has been happening for long years, always, whenever a matter worries me and I want an answer to it, not once in a lifetime.

And before that there was the Yusuf of 2023, when a "blind of insight" described me as having invented a dream and called me a liar. I slept saddened, and I saw the real birth of Allah's Prophet Yusuf, peace be upon him, when he was born .. I was in the house of Allah's Prophet""")

t(13, 60, """Jacob, peace be upon him, standing in the hall of the house, and to our right a room in which his wife was giving birth to Yusuf, peace be upon him. Allah's Prophet Jacob, peace be upon him, was standing in front of me, and one of the older brothers of Allah's Prophet Yusuf, or a relative - a young man, but not a small young man - was standing to my right, and another man, perhaps a brother or a relative, to my left. It was an old, somewhat spacious house, of very old construction, with rugs of wool covering its floor. Then Yusuf, peace be upon him, was born, and they brought him from the room, from his mother. He was given to me before everyone; I took him in my arms, placed him close to my chest and looked at him: round-faced, white, his face almost glowing from his beauty and from the purity and clarity of his good, pure, innocent soul, beautiful with a beauty not seen in any child we have seen in our lives. He looked at me and I looked at him, wrapped in the clothes of a newborn child, a clean white cloth, and he smiled at me. End.

Surah Yusuf is the surah of truly confronting the soul. It is the great message to people to calm down! To overcome desires that do not affect their Hereafter! To resist the soul's share .. To know that Allah's decrees are very specific .. and very exclusive, and that resisting them is challenging Allah the Exalted in His dominion and on His earth and rejecting His decrees, and that no one will do that but destroy himself. Surah Yusuf, where the brothers rejected Allah's decree concerning Yusuf and decided to draw his destiny themselves, and thought they had drawn it when they planned for him to become a slave sold in the slave markets by putting him in a well! Then he became the second man in a great kingdom!

Elevation on earth is a decision from Allah the Exalted alone, and is not sought by mere human desire .. So Surah Yusuf is a message to all people .. Calm down .. Submit to Allah ... Surrender to Allah .. Otherwise there is inevitable disgrace, because the Lord does not accept anyone saying to Him: Why?!

Surah Yusuf is a command from our Great Lord that we meet Him on the Day of Resurrection without having posed in our lives the first question of disbelief: Why him? Why him and not me? The first question of disbelief! The question Iblis said. So where is he today? In a lofty station, or in the lowest of the low?""")

h(13, 1400, """The punishment for injustice is the blotting out of insight! In 2023, the story of an oppressor and the story of an oppressed one who saw the real birth of Allah's Prophet Yusuf!""")

t(13, 2000, """Except Jerusalem, it is the only exception .. Two kingdoms ruling the world from Jerusalem: the Solomonic one has passed, and the other has not yet come!

So where is the return of the other kingdoms of history that arose from various countries and occupied the world?! Muslim and non-Muslim! None of them returned!
The Romans, the English and the French, and of the virtuous kingdoms, the first Caliphate, then the biting kingship up to the Ottoman!

The matter in their not returning is not that they were all wrong. Allah the Great forbid; among them is the first Caliphate from pure, purified Medina. But it is the Sunnah of Allah the Great concerning kingdoms and great states, a Sunnah of which we understand some and are ignorant of some. To Allah, our Great Lord, belongs the far-reaching wisdom, holy are His names and attributes, exalted in the heavens and the earth, and highly exalted, the All-Glorified, the All-Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit.

Medina .. Kufa .. Damascus .. Baghdad .. Cairo .. Istanbul

Cities from which the whole Islamic world, or important parts of it, were ruled""")

t(14, 100, """Cairo: the Fatimids and the Mamluks
Kufa: the whole old Islamic world except the Levant

The capitals of the Islamic states passed away, and those capitals did not return again!""")

h(14, 650, """Many cities had a share of the world's dominion, then dominion never returns to them. The Sunnah of our Great Lord in the great kingdoms""")

t(14, 1345, """How many righteous, patient people and luminaries of the religion are in you, O Yemen! So do not be saddened that one not from you has gone astray in your land. He is one of the emergences of the Dajjal and will not exceed his limit .. A warning against the misguided one of Yemen, the new emergence of the Dajjal .. "Abdulaziz al-Qahtani", who attacks the station of the Chosen One ﷺ and his family, the station of Allah's Prophet Isa, peace be upon him, and the station of his mother the truthful one, peace be upon her. So let him not mislead you, O some of our brothers in Yemen, and bring you down with him where the abysses of ruin await him every hour, for I see a following around him whose breath keeps swelling, and he is nothing but one of the breaths of Satan. Indeed, have I conveyed?""")

h(14, 2000, """How excellent are our brothers, the people of Yemen! And may Allah not bless a misguided one who went astray in its land and attacked the station of my master, the Messenger of Allah""")

t(15, 90, """Establishing the proof and absolving oneself of responsibility before this one who has gone clearly astray

Abdulaziz al-Qahtani's claim that the sons of Imam Ali and Fatima, peace be upon them both, who settled in the land of Canaan sanctify themselves, is a claim written against you and recorded in the record of your deeds; so beautiful patience, and Allah is the One sought for help against what you describe. You declared a whole Muslim people disbelievers, you were racist for your tribalism, and you went the ways of those whose tongues stank. Then you repeated and reiterated your hatred for the family of the House who settled in the land of Canaan, and claimed that those of the family of the House living in the land of Canaan corrupted the religion and ruined Islam, and you swore by the Great Lord that He hates the sons of Fatima and Ali, peace be upon them both, who settled in the land of Canaan!! Wretched, by Allah, is what I heard from an ignorant man saturated with the first Jahiliyyah, and your setting up enmity toward the family of the House of the Messenger of Allah who settled in the land of Canaan. I see you have gone clearly astray and shown enmity to the family of the House of Prophethood openly, in broad daylight. Then you end the evil article seeking support from the Shia, calling them "my brothers!!", asking them to help you so you may seize a dominion your soul desired!! Altering and changing the religion of Allah, saying that our Lord did not command us to obey Muhammad ibn Abdullah but only commanded us to obey the Messenger, scattering the minds of the Muslims with your old heresies, which we previously warned against without naming you. Indeed, your misguidance has revealed worn-out molars, and a lip torn by the thorns of your attack on the station of your master Muhammad ﷺ and his family, with your saying that he has no merit over anyone. He is your master and the crown on your head, and he has merit over you and over your forefathers.

Then you will pay the price of your attack with obscene, filthy words against the Messiah, peace be upon him, and his mother the truthful one, peace be upon her""")

h(15, 1200, """The sons of Ali and Fatima, peace be upon them both, do not plunge into trials, and they know the size of the hostility and enmity, but beautiful patience!""")

t(15, 1810, """A seeker of dominion at the cost of the blood of the Muslims .. His call will destroy you one by one, for (it holds) killing and exemplary punishment. His call is a call Satan breathed into his soul, and he received it and broadcast it. So beware of responding to it, for it is your destruction one by one. As for rising against the rulers individually or collectively, it is forbidden; it is not fitting for you or for others.""")

h(15, 2250, """O people of the Hijaz, beware of the call of the caller to sedition, Abdulaziz al-Qahtani!""")

t(16, 430, """People in this are between one who schemes for himself and one schemed against. So never scheme for yourself, for every scheme is in the Fire; and do not test people. But know that truthfulness with Allah is salvation: whoever is truthful with Allah, He supports him with loved ones, not enemies, then makes him know those who hate him and reveals them to him. As for still water, it is a thought that produces no benefit; but once its features and limits become clear, it produces good and righteousness on earth.""")

h(16, 950, """The fishing line of abundant humility is cast into still water, and it makes a great storm that is clearly seen!""")

t(16, 1615, """Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs""")

h(16, 2050, """A Shariah teacher at the university, fluent of tongue, except that when he mentions the Prophet he says: "sal sallam"!!!!! I do not know where this "sal sallam" came from?!!!!""")

h(17, 500, """The Muslim is assessed by his emotion toward loyalty and disavowal, and the sheikh of religion is assessed by his loyalty and disavowal toward history and its figures""")

h(17, 1600, """A Muslim {and proud of my tawhid}. This is all I am, and I will be nothing else until I die""")

h(18, 250, """A person's thought is a firm mountain that can never be changed""")

t(18, 710, """What does Allah our Great Lord say, and what does His Messenger ﷺ and his family say, in what was revealed to him, about such-and-such jurisprudential issue? And not: "What is your eminence's opinion on such-and-such jurisprudential issue?".

My comment on the correctness of the noble brother's opinion and contribution

The word "opinion" is a dangerous word, and dangerous psychological sediments are built upon it, so people think that issuing fatwas is revelation, while the schools differ in their ijtihad, and it legitimizes the word "opinion"; because of the trial of glorifying the sheikhs, which has struck the Ummah in its feet and hands and bloodied the Ummah's face until it turned black, since almost everything in the Ummah turns out unguided and unsuccessful, and almost every word and deed today is on a path that has nothing to do with Islam.""")

h(18, 1500, """A noble brother sent it to me as audio. O sheikhs, do not accept from people their saying this to you:""")

h(18, 2350, """The Book is taken with strength "to straighten what is crooked" """)
